  "note": "Election of the Cookstown Urban District Council, ordinary day 15 January 1934; the four retiring councillors were declared elected without a contest (Belfast News-Letter, 6 January 1934, p. 7). 'In Cookstown the four retiring councillors — Messrs. Robert E. Balmer, James Wright, Wm. H. Newell, and Wm. Gough — were nominated yesterday, and as there were no other candidates they were duly declared elected.' Returned unopposed."
